          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a shackle, then the Arabic for to release."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: شيد",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شيد — shayyada — \"to erect, to build up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شيد الملك قصرا كبيرا. shayyada al-malik qaṣran kabīran. The king built a great palace."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يشيد, yushayyid."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of grand buildings; بنى is the everyday verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شيد (shayyada) is built on the native Arabic root sh-y-d (Lane), where shīd is plaster and Form II shayyada is \"to plaster a building, to raise it high\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
