              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سيطر — sayṭara — \"to control, to take control\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سيطر رجال الإطفاء على الحريق. sayṭara rijāl al-iṭfāʾ ʿalā al-ḥarīq. The firefighters brought the fire under control."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يسيطر, yusayṭir."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes على: سيطر (sayṭara) على."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سيطر (sayṭara) is filed under the root s-ṭ-r (Lane), the root of saṭr, a line, with muṣayṭir, an overseer. Its earlier history, perhaps through Aramaic, is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
